.TH BREWMASTER 1 "2026-08-11" "brewmaster 0.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brewmaster \- selective Homebrew package upgrades by semver bump level
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brewmaster
\fI[upgrade]\fR \fI[packages...]\fR \fI[options]\fR
.br
.B brewmaster
snapshot \fIsave|list|diff|restore|delete\fR \fI[ref]\fR \fI[options]\fR
.br
.B brewmaster
deps show \fI[package]\fR
.br
.B brewmaster
profile \fIlist|create|edit|diff|validate\fR \fI[args]\fR
.br
.B brewmaster
cleanup \fI[--dry-run|--interactive|--force]\fR
.br
.B brewmaster
why \fIpackage\fR
.br
.B brewmaster
bloat
.br
.B brewmaster
log \fI[--package=NAME]\fR \fI[--action=upgrade|cleanup|snapshot]\fR \fI[--since=Nd]\fR \fI[--format=table|json|csv]\fR
.br
.B brewmaster
report
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brewmaster
upgrades only what you decide \(em patch, minor, or major \(em nothing more.
It classifies every outdated package by its semantic-versioning bump, gates
the upgrade by the requested level, and understands
.I why
a package exists on your machine before touching it.
.PP
brewmaster is deterministic: no AI, no guessing, no network calls beyond
.BR brew (1)
itself. Run
.B brewmaster help
.I command
for a per-command reference, or
.B brewmaster --help
for the full flag reference.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS UPGRADE (default command)
.TP
.B upgrade \fI[packages...]\fR
Selective upgrade by semver bump level.
Pass package names to limit the upgrade to those:
e.g. brewmaster upgrade git node --minor
.PP
.B Level (mutually exclusive; default: patch):
.TP
.B --patch
Apply patch bumps only (default).
.TP
.B --minor
Apply minor bumps only.
.TP
.B --major
Apply major bumps only.
.TP
.B --level=patch|minor|major
Same as the flags above (also: --level minor).
.PP
.B Flags:
.TP
.B --or-lower
Make it inclusive (e.g. --minor => minor+patch; --major => all).
.TP
.B --allow-date
Treat date versions (YYYY.MM.DD / YYYY-MM-DD...) as semver-like. Default: false.
.TP
.B -n, --dry-run
Show the plan without executing.
.TP
.B --formulae
Formulae only (skip casks).
.TP
.B --casks
Casks only (skip formulae).
.TP
.B --profile=NAME
Filter/level from a named profile (see PROFILES).
.TP
.B --interactive, -i
No effect (review below is now always shown; kept for compatibility).
Before executing, candidates are always shown for review: fzf multi-select if
installed, else a table plus a single \fI[y/N]\fR for the whole batch. --dry-run and
--yes both skip this (--dry-run shows the table and stops; --yes upgrades all).
.SS DEPENDENCY RISK
.TP
.B deps show \fI[package]\fR
Show dependency risk for one package, or list all
outdated packages sorted by risk score.
e.g. brewmaster deps show node
.PP
.B Flags (apply to upgrade):
.TP
.B --check-deps
Risk-score each upgrade candidate; skip HIGH-risk, warn on MEDIUM.
.TP
.B --risk-threshold=N
HIGH-risk cutoff (default: 7; range 0-10).
.TP
.B --yes, -y
Auto-confirm MEDIUM-risk packages, and skip the upgrade review step.
.SS SNAPSHOT & ROLLBACK
.TP
.B snapshot save
Save current Homebrew state to a snapshot.
.TP
.B snapshot list
List all snapshots.
.TP
.B snapshot diff \fI[INDEX|PATH]\fR
Show packages changed since a snapshot.
.TP
.B snapshot restore \fI[INDEX|PATH]\fR
Restore packages to a snapshot state.
.TP
.B snapshot delete \fI[INDEX|PATH]\fR
Delete a snapshot.
e.g. brewmaster snapshot restore 0
.PP
.B Flags:
.TP
.B --label=TEXT
Label for 'snapshot save'.
.TP
.B -n, --dry-run
Show plan without executing for 'snapshot restore'.
.TP
.B --force
Skip the y/N confirmation for 'snapshot delete'.
.SS PROFILES
.TP
.B profile list
List configured profiles.
.TP
.B profile create
Interactive wizard to add a new profile.
.TP
.B profile edit \fI[name]\fR
Open profiles.toml in $EDITOR.
.TP
.B profile diff \fIa\fR \fIb\fR
Compare include lists between two profiles.
.TP
.B profile validate
Check profiles.toml for errors.
e.g. brewmaster upgrade --profile=work
.PP
.B Flags (apply to upgrade):
.TP
.B --profile=NAME
Apply a profile's package filter and level.
.TP
.B --interactive, -i
No effect (upgrade always reviews candidates before executing).
.SS CLEANUP & INTENT
.TP
.B cleanup
Report orphan/stale/pinned-old formulae (read-only by default).
.TP
.B why \fIpackage\fR
Explain why a formula is installed (dependents,
install date, last-access heuristic).
.TP
.B bloat
Summary of installed package counts and estimated
disk reclaim from cleanup candidates.
e.g. brewmaster cleanup --interactive
.PP
.B Flags (apply to cleanup):
.TP
.B -n, --dry-run
Read-only report (also the default with no flags).
.TP
.B --interactive, -i
fzf multi-select packages to remove (requires fzf).
.TP
.B --force
Auto-remove orphans with cleanup score >= 7, no confirmation.
.SS AUDIT LOG & REPORTS
.TP
.B log
Show recent audit log entries (last 20 by default).
.TP
.B report
Machine health summary: upgrades, cleanups,
snapshots, orphans, and risk trend.
e.g. brewmaster log --action=upgrade --since=7d
.PP
.B Flags (apply to log):
.TP
.B --package=NAME
Filter entries by package name.
.TP
.B --action=ACTION
Filter by action: upgrade|cleanup|snapshot.
.TP
.B --since=Nd|Nh|Nw
Only entries within this time window (default unit: days).
.TP
.B --format=table|json|csv
Output format (default: table).
.SS GENERAL
.TP
.B -v, --verbose
More detailed output.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show this help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/brewmaster/snapshots/
Snapshots stored in. (XDG_DATA_HOME respected).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/brewmaster/audit.log
Audit log stored in. (XDG_DATA_HOME respected).
.TP
.I ~/.config/brewmaster/profiles.toml
Profiles read from. (XDG_CONFIG_HOME respected).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B brewmaster upgrade git node --minor
.TP
.B brewmaster deps show node
.TP
.B brewmaster snapshot restore 0
.TP
.B brewmaster upgrade --profile=work
.TP
.B brewmaster cleanup --interactive
.TP
.B brewmaster log --action=upgrade --since=7d
